## 3. Review dimensions (in priority order)

### 3.1 Platform-guard correctness — HIGHEST VALUE

Compile-time macros in use: `RDKB_SUPPORT`, `RDKB_EXTENDER_SUPPORT`, `RDKC`, `GTEST_ENABLE`,
`LIBRDKCERTSELECTOR`, `LIBRDKCONFIG_BUILD`, `IARMBUS_SUPPORT`.

Check every changed hunk for:

- **Asymmetric edits.** A fix applied in the `#ifdef RDKB_SUPPORT` branch but not in the `#else`
  (video/STB) branch, or vice versa. Example of a real divergence in this file: `GetServURL()`
  consults `rfc_state` only under `RDKB_SUPPORT`; `GetStoredHashAndTime()` skips the
  `rfc_state == Init` / `isXconfSelectorSlotProd()` check only under `RDKC`.
- **Path constants that differ per platform.** `RFC_PROPERTIES_PERSISTENCE_FILE` is
  `/nvram/rfc.properties` (RDKB) vs `/opt/rfc.properties` (video/RDKC);
  `RFC_REBOOT_CRON_SCRIPT` is `/etc/RfcRebootCronschedule.sh` (RDKB) vs
  `/lib/rdk/RfcRebootCronschedule.sh` (RDKC) and is undefined elsewhere. A new
  hard-coded path is a defect unless it is genuinely platform-neutral.
- **Members / helpers used outside their guard.** A field declared under `#ifdef RDKC`
  (e.g. `_rfcRebootCronNeeded`, `_effectiveImmediateParams`) referenced from unguarded code
  breaks the video and broadband builds.
- **Query-parameter drift.** `CreateXconfHTTPUrl()` emits `osClass` and `Experience` only for
  video/STB but `experience` (lowercase) for RDKB/RDKC, and `accountMgmt`/`serialNum` only for
  `RDKB_EXTENDER_SUPPORT`. Changing casing or ordering breaks server-side matching rules.
- **`GTEST_ENABLE` path redirection.** `BOOTSTRAP_FILE`, `PARTNER_ID_FILE`,
  `DEVICE_PROPERTIES_FILE` switch to `/tmp/...` under gtest. New production paths must get the
  same treatment or unit tests will touch real system files.

For each finding, state explicitly **which platforms are affected: video/STB, broadband (RDKB),
extender, camera (RDKC)**.

### 3.2 Memory safety

Target the C/C++ defect classes that actually bite this codebase:

- `DownloadData` / `HeaderDwnLoc` buffers: `allocDowndLoadDataMem()` must be paired with
  `free(pvOut)` on **every** path, including early `break`/`continue` in the retry loop.
- `cJSON` objects from `ParseJsonStr()` must reach `FreeJson()`; watch for early `return` between
  parse and free, and for freeing a parent while a child pointer is still in use.
- `strcpy`/`strcat`/`sprintf`/`strtok` on fixed buffers — require `snprintf` with `sizeof(dst)` and
  explicit NUL termination. Check every `char buf[N]` introduced by the diff.
- `popen`/`v_secure_system`/`v_secure_popen` — verify `pclose`, and verify no untrusted string
  (Xconf response value, TR-181 value, partner ID, account ID) is interpolated into the command.
- Returning pointers/references to stack or to `std::string` temporaries (`.c_str()` on a temporary).
- Ownership after `std::move` — the moved-from `std::string` must not be read again.

### 3.3 Thread safety

- `rfcMgr` forks in `rfc_main.cpp` and uses signal handlers: only async-signal-safe calls are legal
  inside a handler; flags must be `volatile sig_atomic_t`.
- IARM/rbus event callbacks run on a different thread than the main processing loop — any member
  they touch needs a mutex or must be immutable.
- Flag non-reentrant libc use (`strtok`, `getenv` + write, `localtime`, static buffers) on any path
  reachable from more than one thread.
- Flag lock-order changes, locks held across blocking I/O (curl, file writes), and early returns
  that skip an unlock (prefer RAII `std::lock_guard`).

### 3.4 Behavioural contracts (XConf / TR-181 / IARM / mTLS)

- **XConf:** `configSetHash` / `configSetTime` round-trip must stay consistent. Sentinels
  `OVERRIDE_HASH`, `UPGRADE_HASH`, `CLEARED`, and time `"0"` have specific meanings; changing when
  they are emitted changes server-side 304 behaviour. Firmware-version change must force
  `UPGRADE_HASH` and `_is_first_request`.
- **TR-181:** parameter names are contracts. Verify exact spelling of
  `Device.DeviceInfo.X_RDKCENTRAL-COM_RFC.*` strings; a typo silently no-ops on device.
  Check that `tr181.list`, `rfcFeature.list`, `rfcVariable.ini`, and `tr181store.ini` writes stay
  atomic (temp file + rename) and survive power loss.
- **Effective-immediate vs reboot:** `effectiveImmediate == false` must set `isRebootRequired`;
  `true` must apply without reboot. Do not let a change silently invert this — it either causes
  unexpected reboots in the field or features that never take effect.
- **Maintenance Manager:** `isMaintenanceEnabled()` gates reboot scheduling; reboot must not be
  triggered directly when maintenance manager owns the window.
- **mTLS:** cert selection must keep the retry/fallback order (dynamic XPKI → static XPKI) and must
  never log certificate paths, passphrases, key material, account ID, or full MAC. Check
  `LIBRDKCERTSELECTOR` guarded code against the non-selector fallback.
- **Secrets in logs:** any new `RDK_LOG` printing an Xconf response value, account ID, partner ID,
  or URL with credentials is a finding.

### 3.5 Test coverage of the change

- Every changed function in `rfcMgr/`, `rfcapi/`, `tr181api/`, `utils/` should have a corresponding
  L1 gtest in `rfcMgr/gtest/` or `test/` (`run_ut.sh`).
- Behaviour visible over the Xconf wire or through TR-181 should have an L2 test
  (`test/functional-tests/`, `run_l2.sh`, `run_l2_reboot_trigger.sh`, mock-xconf artifacts in
  `test/test-artifacts/mockxconf/`).
- Name the **specific** missing test: file, suggested test-case name, and what it should assert.
  If the PR changes a state transition, require a test that asserts the resulting `rfc_state`.
- Flag tests that were deleted or disabled without a stated reason.

### 3.6 Build system impact

- New source file → must be added to the correct `Makefile.am` `_SOURCES`.
- New `-D` flag → must come from a `configure.ac` `AC_ARG_ENABLE` + `AM_CONDITIONAL` + `AC_SUBST`,
  not hard-coded in `CXXFLAGS`.
- New external dependency → `PKG_CHECK_MODULES` and the matching `_LDADD`/`_CPPFLAGS`.
- Changing a guard name in code without updating `configure.ac` (or vice versa) is a defect.
- Check that a new `#ifdef` does not break the gtest build configured with `--enable-gtestapp`.

